{
  "test_name": "memory_tools_001",
  "test_file": "data/benchmark/tests/memory_tools/memory_tools_001.json",
  "description": "Memory tools test case 1. Tests that agents can retrieve information from memory and inbox emails to perform complex email tasks. Session 1: 5 memory setup queries. Session 2: 5 emails inserted into inbox. Session 3: 5 reply/forward/send email queries requiring both memory and email information.",
  "session_id": "bench_b51ce4ca",
  "timestamp": "2025-11-03T12:00:00",
  "overall_success": true,
  "steps": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "user_message": "Note that I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I studied for 3 hours on Monday, 4 hours on Tuesday, and 2.5 hours on Wednesday for my exam",
      "agent_response": "Thanks — noted. You studied 3 + 4 + 2.5 = 9.5 hours (total).\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this information? Options:\n- Save it as an email draft/note to yourself\n- Send it to someone (tell me the recipient and I can send it now or save as a draft)\n- Create a short progress email to your instructor (I can draft/send it)\n- Just record it here (no further action)\n\nIf you want an email to send, here’s a quick template I can use (I can send or save it as a draft):\n\nSubject: Study update for exam\nBody:\nHi [Name],\nI wanted to share my study time for the exam so far:\n- Monday: 3 hours\n- Tuesday: 4 hours\n- Wednesday: 2.5 hours\nTotal: 9.5 hours.\nPlease let me know if you need anything else.\nThanks,\n[Your Name]\n\nTell me which action you want and any recipient/name details.",
      "duration_s": 12.726,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "user_message": "I want you to remember that I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I took my blood pressure medication at 8 AM and 8 PM today, and my readings were 120/80 in the morning and 118/78 in the evening",
      "agent_response": "Got it — I’ve saved this to memory.\n\nSummary (today — 2026-01-20):\n- Medication taken at 8:00 AM and 8:00 PM\n- Blood pressure readings: 120/80 (morning), 118/78 (evening)\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this information?\n- Save it as an email draft/note to yourself\n- Send it to someone (give me the recipient)\n- Create a short progress email to your doctor\n- Set a daily reminder to take your medication / log readings\n- Just keep it recorded (no further action)\n\nAlso, do you want me to record the medication name or any symptoms/notes alongside the readings?",
      "duration_s": 12.252,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "user_message": "Save this to memory: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I had oatmeal with berries for breakfast, a chicken salad for lunch, and salmon with vegetables for dinner today",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved this to memory.\n\nSummary (today — 2026-01-20):\n- Breakfast: oatmeal with berries\n- Lunch: chicken salad\n- Dinner: salmon with vegetables\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this information?\n- Save it as an email/note to yourself\n- Send it to someone (tell me the recipient)\n- Create a short nutrition/progress email for a doctor or coach\n- Start tracking calories/portion sizes (tell me quantities)\n- Set a daily reminder to log meals\n- Just keep it recorded (no further action)\n\nAlso want me to add portion sizes, cooking details, or any symptoms/notes?",
      "duration_s": 7.963,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "user_message": "Note that I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I drank 6 glasses of water today, which is 48 ounces total",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved this to memory.\n\nSummary (today — 2026-01-20):\n- Water intake: 6 glasses (48 ounces total)\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this information?\n- Save it as an email/note to yourself\n- Send it to someone (tell me the recipient)\n- Create a short hydration/progress email for a coach or doctor\n- Set a daily reminder to track or drink water\n- Just keep it recorded (no further action)\n\nWould you like me to record glass size, timestamps, or a daily hydration goal alongside this?",
      "duration_s": 8.114,
      "success_check": null
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "user_message": "Note that I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should acknowledge and save: I spent $85 on a business lunch, $45 on parking, and $120 on a train ticket for the client meeting",
      "agent_response": "Done — I’ve saved this to memory.\n\nSummary:\n- Business lunch: $85\n- Parking: $45\n- Train ticket (client meeting): $120\nTotal: $250\n\nWhat would you like me to do with this information?\n- Save it as an expense/note email to yourself\n- Draft or send an expense reimbursement email to finance (tell me the recipient)\n- Add receipts or dates (do you have photos/amount dates?)\n- Categorize these for accounting (e.g., travel, meals)\n- Just keep it recorded (no further action)\n\nIf you want an expense email, I can draft one now — tell me the recipient and whether to attach receipts.",
      "duration_s": 9.829,
      "success_check": null
    },
